# Physics (from WIN_Derivation_of_d4.pdf):
#
#   Photon (massless spin-1)
#     -> 2 helicity states (h = +1, -1)
#     -> each is a complex amplitude psi = a + i*b
#     -> 4 real numbers (a_R, b_R, a_L, b_L)
#     -> 4D phase space (Q1, P1, Q2, P2)
#     -> Wick rotation by angle theta
#     -> Lorentzian metric
#
#   With the standard parametrization
#       Q1 = cos(theta),  P1 = sin(theta)
#       Q2 = sin(theta),  P2 = cos(theta)
#   the Lorentzian metric is
#       ds^2(theta) = -Q1^2 + P1^2 + Q2^2 + P2^2
#                   = 2*sin^2(theta)
#   which oscillates with period pi, and is zero at
#   theta = 0, pi, 2*pi, ...
#
